Benefits and risks of AI coding agents to software developers
 

1. Faster coding
AI can generate code suggestions and help developers complete programming tasks more quickly.


2. Increased productivity
AI can help developers complete certain tasks with less manual effort.


3. Reduced repetitive work
AI can assist with routine coding tasks, allowing developers to focus on more complex problems.


4. Improved developer experience
AI assistance can reduce frustration and make some coding tasks more enjoyable.


5. Assistance with unfamiliar code
AI can help developers understand code and explore possible solutions, although its explanations must be checked.






Risks of AI Coding Agents

1. Security vulnerabilities
AI-generated code may introduce security problems if developers do not review and test it.


2. Incorrect code
AI can produce code that looks correct but contains mistakes or unsafe behaviour.


3. Reduced productivity
Developers may spend extra time checking and correcting AI-generated code.


4. Privacy concerns
Sensitive information may be exposed when AI tools process confidential data.


5. Overdependence on AI
Developers may rely too heavily on AI suggestions rather than practising independent problem-solving.
Related concern; needs a separate supporting study

6. Inconsistent performance
AI tools may help with some programming tasks but slow developers down on others.

